WEBVTT

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.480
The So Army

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.330
So.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.860
The Gi Army

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:11.410
Gi.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.240
The En Army

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:12.540
En.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.610
The Kan Army

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:13.830
Kan.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:14.990
The Se Army

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.120
Se.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.370
The Sho Army

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.500
Sho.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.040
A coalition army made up of
these six nations began its invasion,

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.700
preparing to rain down unprecedented
calamity upon the kingdom of Chin.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:24.870
A coalition army!

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.370
But word of the mass invasion
had not yet reached the Hi Shin Force.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.560
A Coming Together

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:08.120
Hold!

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:10.910
A reply from the King of Se!

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:14.700
He grants you an audience.
You may pass through each gate!

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:15.790
Is this true?

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:20.500
That King of Se--he's a quick one.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:28.000
And how fortuitous! I just happened to have been
stationed here in the east.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:28.040
One of Ryo 
Fuis FourPillars 

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.130
Kanyou, Kingdom of Chin

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:32.830
I see.

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:36.160
So we go after Se, eh?

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:37.160
Yes.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:42.290
The Se army has yet to reach Chin's borders.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:45.330
We will use Sai Taku's talents in diplomacy

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.750
to make Se separate from the coalition army.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:52.150
Royal Capital 
of the Kingdom of Se

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:57.330
S-Sai Taku, sir...

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:02.330
Can this audience really result
in Se leaving the coalition army?

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:05.830
Even I cannot be certain.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:11.830
The current Se King has his quirks, you see--
he can be quite difficult to read.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:17.250
Then again, perhaps it's thanks to
his quirks that we have an audience at all.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:26.350
King of Se

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:26.080
Ah, Sai Taku. 'S been a while.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:29.950
Oh, this?

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:35.120
This is a venomous snake, roasted whole.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:37.910
Try it. It's terrible.

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:41.160
No, that's wrong: I meant "It energizes you."

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:45.410
So?

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:48.580
Chin is surrounded on all sides
by the invading coalition army.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:52.830
What business could Sai Taku, diplomat of Chin,
a country on the brink of extinction,

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.660
have with me, the King of Se?

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:02.540
By all means, speak your mind.

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:06.000
You and I, we go quite far back, after all.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.080
And I am rather short on time myself.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:15.330
I've slowed the Se army's pace
so we could have this meeting.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:21.080
Our army lags behind the other five;
I may order them to speed up or to stop.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.950
That will depend entirely
on what you have to say.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:28.830
A sobering thought indeed!

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.450
Permit me to be candid:

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:35.540
I am certain you know
of Sho's chancellor, Ri Boku.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.910
When he bought you, how much did he pay?

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:44.120
How dare you!

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:46.250
You would ridicule our King?!

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:56.160
You see, Sai Taku, war is just another job,
a means of earning riches.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:02.370
That it is. Which is why I ask:

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:05.950
How much did he pay?

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.200
I don't know the specifics.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:16.410
According to Ri Boku, the land, valuables,
and people won in the war

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:21.830
would be divvied up among each
participating army according to its scale.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:27.200
A rough estimate, then,
of what you stand to profit if you capture

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.750
the entirety of Chin.

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:34.250
I, Sai Taku, promise you twice that sum.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.040
Tw- <i>Twice</i> ?

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:41.290
Oh? On what condition?

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:46.660
Se withdraws from the coalition army.
That is all.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:48.700
You've made quite the blunder, Sai Taku!

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:57.120
Why, I would have done as much
<i>without</i> your offer of twice the pay.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.830
No backing out now.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:01.450
Y-Your Highness!

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:06.330
Send a bird to General Gan Mo:
Withdraw the army and turn back.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:08.290
And a messenger by fast horse to Ri Boku:

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:12.000
A sudden illness has made me unfit to wage war.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:15.540
A-Are you sure it will be that simple?

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:18.000
Surely Ri Boku will have some choice words...

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:22.660
Twice the sum, without using
a single soldier. What a deal!

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:27.950
Besides, I've known Sai Taku
for much longer than I have Ri Boku.

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:29.580
Isn't that right, Sai Taku?

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.870
How very kind of you.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.580
Ready that horse!

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:35.750
We'll need countermeasures!

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:37.080
Yes, some kind of plan.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:37.870
Yes, yes.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.410
Ri Boku is a monster.

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:47.120
That's what I thought when we met in secret.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:50.830
His defeating the likes of Ou Ki
and Geki Shin was no fluke.

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:55.950
To be frank, withdrawing our forces
will do little to reduce his power.

00:06:55.950 --> 00:07:01.950
Chin has a one in a million chance
of besting Ri Boku's coalition army.

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:04.160
I am all too aware.

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:08.120
But this is the extent of what diplomacy can do.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:11.620
All that remains is to trust our countryfolk.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:12.110
Kanyou, Kingdom of Chin

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:18.330
A bird from Sai Taku! Se has withdrawn!

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:19.790
--I-Is this true?
--Outstanding!

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.160
--Fifty thousand Se troops--and no fighting?
--We did it!

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:24.250
--Hooray for Sai Taku!
--And it only took one meeting!

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:27.910
Just a moment!
This is no time to be celebrating!

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:32.330
Certainly I'm glad Se's 50,000 troops
are no longer an issue...

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:33.660
The thing is...

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.790
The war situation remains largely unchanged.

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:42.410
Reducing the enemy's combat potential
wasn't the sole reason for removing Se.

