00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:09.330
But can this dire situation go on
long enough to be a drawn-out war?

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:13.660
The Gi army has advanced the furthest
and requires the most urgency.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:16.720
Chiku

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:16.720
Rai plains

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:16.720
Gi army

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:17.500
I expect they've passed Rai plains by now.

00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:21.450
Realistically, we can only stop
the Gi army at Chiku.

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:23.080
Chiku?

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:25.290
They're so far into the interior...

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:27.330
Urgent report!

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:31.080
We know the Gi army's position!
They're still in Rai plains!

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:32.250
Rai plains?!

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:34.250
They haven't passed it by?

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:37.580
I don't know the details, but one of our armies,
acting on its own authority,

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:40.000
has engaged the Gi army in Rai plains!

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:41.790
On its own authority?!

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:43.950
Judging by the report, their general is...

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.700
Feel that? The fightin' has already begun!

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:55.120
The Gi army and the Chin army
are crossin' swords!

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:57.000
The Chin army's outnumbered...

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.200
But they've got nearly 10,000.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:02.200
Are you stupid? Gi has 100,000!

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:05.750
I knew it. Headquarters acted too slowly!

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:06.950
That army...

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:10.040
Are they trying to stop
the 100,000-man Gi army?

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:12.830
Th-That's so reckless!

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:14.950
No... they're actually doing...

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.540
...surprisingly well!

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:17.790
Wait...

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:19.620
Wh-Who <i>are</i> they, anyway?!

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:24.500
They're crazy strong!

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:26.120
I-Is that...

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:31.250
Lord Hyou!

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:33.660
A battalion's trying to break through from the left!

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:35.410
Looking to come here?

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:39.790
Ridiculous. They could never get
this far with such a basic attack.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:41.410
Don't underestimate them, Shu Hi.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:44.390
That's Lord Hyou.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:48.230
Commanding General of Gi

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:48.790
The man who killed my father, Go Kei.

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:53.040
Still, as reported, he's playing
this exceedingly straight.

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:56.080
Shu Hi, aim for their driving force in the rear.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:58.250
We'll come up on either side

00:09:58.250 --> 00:09:59.620
and crush them!

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:10.000
And the enemy's momentum is slowed,
just like that!

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:16.120
We're headin' in, too--

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:18.330
as Lord Hyou's reinforcements!

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:21.700
Who the hell are <i>you</i> ?!

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:23.040
Aim for the wheels!

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:28.290
To the right!

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:29.370
Sir!

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:31.370
Wipe out their right-hand force!

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:36.080
Our pincer attack has fallen apart!

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:38.580
Uh-oh. Their momentum's picking up again!

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:42.910
Follow Lord Hyou!

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:47.040
Hou Mei, sir, let's tighten up
our defensive wall!

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.450
No--not that.

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:51.580
Let's try something more interesting.

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:07.370
The enemy's main army is on the move.
Are they runnin' already?

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:12.000
Ka Ryo Ten! Has their main camp... run off?

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:13.700
No... I guess not.

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:16.910
But why are they in the middle
of their troops and not behind them?

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:21.330
What <i>is</i> all this?

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:23.080
They've assumed an unusual position.

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:26.290
Don't matter!
You're not gettin' away, main camp!

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:28.410
All troops, halt!

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:29.620
What the--

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.540
It stinks to high heaven up ahead.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.290
We're turning back!

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:37.290
Huh?

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:42.200
The Chin army stopped?

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:48.290
Odd, Gi should be out of
well-known generals by now.

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:53.290
That main camp is giving off
the stench of some serious strategy.

00:11:53.290 --> 00:11:57.000
Is a new flame set to spark off?

00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:01.500
The fire at our headquarters is burning out.
Return to give aid!

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:02.500
Sir!

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:07.910
Hou Mei, sir! Lord Hyou's army is withdrawing!

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:09.450
Strange.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:14.500
It's our first time attempting
this flowing-force tactic, and yet...

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.080
...he saw it coming?

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:19.910
No. He couldn't have.

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:25.370
The only other person who could
recognize that move is Ri Boku.

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:28.450
Are we not going after them?

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:30.000
Let them go.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.500
That tactic did a number on our own formation.

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:34.790
We must regroup.

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:44.870
Guess I kept you waiting.

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:49.160
Thanks for your help earlier,
young battalion commander.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:52.080
H-He's even bigger than I thought!

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:55.620
This man is practically a beast...

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.450
Did you get an explanation
of all that's going on?

00:12:58.450 --> 00:13:03.620
Er, yes! There's this coalition army
bearin' down on us.

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:05.950
I've been on and off the battlefield
for many a year,

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:08.500
but I've never seen such a massive invasion.

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:12.750
One false step and the country of Chin
may well cease to exist.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:15.500
C-Chin... cease to exist?!

00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:22.250
It's all up to how our headquarters
in Kanyou responds--

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:26.000
but first we'll have to buy them time.

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:32.700
Join in my battles for a while,
battalion commander.

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:37.580
We'll find a way to stop the Gi army here,
with these troops.

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:41.410
That's our job right now,
as men on the front lines.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:56.940
Chin's Lord Hyou Army vs. Gi's Hou Mei Army: Day 4

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:52.660
Orders from Lord Hyou!

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:57.330
The Hi Shin Force is to attack the enemy's side
from the Shourai mountain path!

00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:58.580
Orders received!

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:00.330
The Shourai mountain path?

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:01.790
Let's go, Hi Shin Force!

00:14:11.290 --> 00:14:14.750
Something's off, Shin!
There are no enemies in this direction.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:16.500
Did the messenger mess up?

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.330
Don't sweat it!

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:21.540
Lord Hyou's fightin' style
has no rhyme or reason.

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:24.450
That battle I was in four years back
at Dakan Plain?

00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:27.200
He took down that shrewd general, Go Kei!

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:30.790
And besides... he had Ou Ki's approval.

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:31.830
There!

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.830
Yep, that general's a real instinctual type!

00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:37.620
Get back, Ten!

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:39.080
It's the Gi army!

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:40.500
An ambush unit?

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:42.540
There's a lot of 'em!

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:45.750
Who cares? We eat right through their flank!

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:51.500
Sand clouds in the mountains to the left...

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:55.080
Has my ambush unit been spotted
going after the rear?

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:59.620
The rumors were right:
Lord Hyou's army truly is an unusual foe.

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:02.330
The placement of each unit,
the way they fight...

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.660
As though everything were reversed,
and tactics forbidden in every strategy manual

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:07.750
were fair game.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:11.050
"Chin"

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:11.540
His men are dying meaningless deaths.

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:12.660
And yet--

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:18.040
In return, they win unlikely victories
at every key point,

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:21.120
thus making up the difference.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:23.810
"Hyou"

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:24.870
If all that truly is just intuition,

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:28.040
this opponent is no laughing matter
for a strategist.

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:30.750
I see how he killed my father.

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:35.660
If we mobilize our central army,
we can send that little squad flying!

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:38.080
Our main forces would see bloodshed.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:41.660
Besides, I rarely have the chance
to face an enemy like this.

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:42.910
Let's just--

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:53.410
All troops, pull back!
We withdraw to Chiku!

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:55.660
We're retreating?!

00:15:57.870 --> 00:16:01.870
So the Sho army's come this far already...

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:02.190
"Sho"

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:06.200
Hou Mei, sir! The Chin army has withdrawn!

00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:08.700
Leave them be.

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:11.750
This man interests me more.

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:23.500
I am Ri Boku, commanding general of the Sho army.

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.910
I seem to have interfered in your battle.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.670
"Gi"

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:28.290
I offer my heartfelt apologies.

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:30.910
He has an open face.

00:16:30.910 --> 00:16:34.120
No coercion, no ulterior motive
behind his smile.

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:38.750
This is the Ri Boku whom every nation is watching.

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:42.160
Go Hou Mei, commanding general
of the Gi army.

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:45.000
But what brings you here?

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:48.620
The armies' rendezvous point is still up ahead.

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:51.370
Has the Sho army changed their route?

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:55.870
No, the main Sho camp
is continuing on ahead of us.

00:16:55.870 --> 00:16:59.750
I was following the Gi army,
so only I came here.

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:03.160
You conquered Goryou
and all its challenges with such ease--

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:06.580
I wondered why you were wasting
several days here, of all places.

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:12.500
The coalition army agreement
<i>does</i> state that we begin

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:15.120
with a <i>swift</i> invasion by <i>all</i> armies.

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:17.950
What's all this?! Why, our general is only--

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:19.290
Wait.

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:22.830
First allow me to clarify, Ri Boku.

00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:25.870
You were indeed the one
who drew up this agreement,

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:29.120
but we are not necessarily subordinate to you.

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:32.540
The Gi and Sho armies are on equal footing.

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:37.790
You are not my superior; it's not your place
to say anything about this army.

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:39.410
Tch!

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:41.830
You're absolutely right.

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:44.330
He didn't bite. I suppose he wouldn't.

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:49.660
But even this is starting to bring
Ri Boku's fighting style into relief.

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:52.580
We have remained here for two reasons.

00:17:52.580 --> 00:17:57.370
First, intel suggests our Gi army
is further along than the others.

00:17:57.370 --> 00:18:02.660
In other words, as the vanguard,
we mustn't shed more blood than the rest.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:06.950
Second, this Lord Hyou fellow
is simply an amusing opponent.

00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:10.040
You certainly are honest with your reasons.

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:13.080
I have some questions for you myself, Ri Boku.

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:20.080
I understand that you want
each army to invade quickly.

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:23.040
That way, we paralyze the Chin army headquarters.

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:26.410
But regardless of whether
that paralysis lasts or fades,

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:29.000
this war is already as good as won.

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:33.250
Indeed it is.

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:40.000
Then I wonder <i>why</i> you'd put together
such a large-scale coalition army

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:42.120
for no real reason.

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:46.870
But I'd like to make certain
of something else first:

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:50.250
How long do you intend this war to go on?

00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:57.000
Until the country of Chin has perished, of course.

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:02.370
He means it, the fiend.

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:15.910
Out...

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:19.790
Outstanding!

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:32.660
So? Come up with a sound strategy?

00:19:35.580 --> 00:19:41.160
We start out in checkmate.
There <i>is</i> no sound strategy for that.

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:43.790
I've run simulations using all sorts of tactics,

00:19:43.790 --> 00:19:48.330
but they all end with the fall
of Kanyou in a hundred battles.

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:53.700
Yet there <i>is</i> one plan that gives
off a faint glimmer of hope...

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:57.370
Oh? How did that simulation turn out?

00:19:57.370 --> 00:20:02.040
Out of a hundred battles, Chin takes 20,
and the coalition army takes 80.

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:09.500
One in five, eh?

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:13.950
Yes--excellent. As a gamble, it will serve well.

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:16.540
A fine job, Shou Hei Kun.

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:18.950
Our armies will stay where they're stationed.

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:22.500
Please summon the generals here to Kanyou.

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:24.540
Which ones?

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:28.330
Every prominent general in the service of Chin.

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:32.910
With the coalition army invading from all sides,

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:38.200
Chin was losing a great number of castles
over a wide area, one after another.

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:43.160
Leaving their homes and land behind,
the people of Chin pressed ever onward

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:45.200
into the country's interior.

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:46.580
A coalition army...

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:48.040
On the attack...

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:51.250
How... how could this happen?

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:53.620
Oh, no... we forgot.

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:54.120
Eh?

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:58.750
In King Sho's day, Chin was the aggressor,
more often than not.

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:04.000
So we had peace of mind--but forgot one
important thing along the way.

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:05.620
Wh-What's that?

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:09.870
The Middle Kingdom has always been
about survival of the fittest-- eat or be eaten.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:14.700
We forgot that there's no guarantee
that Chin won't be eaten!

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:16.950
Eaten? You mean...

00:21:16.950 --> 00:21:19.040
Destroyed!

00:21:20.620 --> 00:21:25.750
Everything depends on
this country's military strength...

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:50.200
So many honorable men, all in one place!

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:52.950
It's so tense in here, it's hard to breathe.

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:56.040
Come to think of it,
this is our first such gathering.

00:21:58.250 --> 00:22:01.790
We've all been briefed on the coalition army.

00:22:01.790 --> 00:22:04.450
Skip the excess formalities
and get this underway.

00:22:04.450 --> 00:22:10.950
Some of us have left our troops behind
to be here today.

00:22:10.950 --> 00:22:12.790
I'm well aware.

00:22:12.790 --> 00:22:13.830
Shou Hei Kun.

00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:14.830
Sir.

00:22:18.200 --> 00:22:22.750
As you know, we are being invaded by
a coalition army of some 500,000 troops.

00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:26.830
Chin is facing a national crisis.

00:22:26.830 --> 00:22:31.160
The coalition army is powerful;
it would take all Chin has to defend against it.

00:22:31.160 --> 00:22:37.160
Which means all of you great generals here
must fight with concentrated might.

00:22:37.160 --> 00:22:40.410
This is literally all-out war--

00:22:40.410 --> 00:22:44.120
if we fail, Chin may well vanish
from the Middle Kingdom entirely!

00:22:46.450 --> 00:22:50.080
Fuuman Plains

00:22:56.810 --> 00:22:58.770
"En"

00:23:03.650 --> 00:23:06.150
"So"

00:23:06.160 --> 00:23:08.650
"Kan"

00:23:17.370 --> 00:23:19.040
Now...

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:20.870
Let me explain our strategy.

